<title>SWEDEN: Orrefors plans rationalisation talks with unions.</title>
<headline>Orrefors plans rationalisation talks with unions.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The new owners of Swedish luxury glass maker Orrefors Kosta Boda on Tuesday said the company was to start talks with unions over rationalisation.</p>
<p>The company late last year was taken over by a specially formed consortium, Orrefors Kosta Boda Holding AB (OKB), that involves Swedish investment group Proventus AB, Danish luxury goods maker Royal Copenhagen A/S and Scandinavian Equity Partners (SEP).</p>
<p>SEP in turn is owned by S-E-Banken, Investor AB U.S. private investment company AEA Investors Inc and by management.</p>
</text>
